-RKL01-0001-Rocket_Lab_PREFIRE_1_Launch_1080p-M6988/collection.json","data":[{"album":["Rocket_Lab_PREFIRE"],"center":"KSC","date_created":"2024-05-25T00:00:00Z","description":"A Rocket Lab Electron rocket lifts off from Launch Complex 1 in Māhia, New Zealand at 7:41 p.m. NZST (3:41 a.m. EDT) Saturday, May 25, 2024, on the first of two launches which Rocket Lab named “Ready, Aim, PREFIRE,” for NASA’s PREFIRE (Polar Radiant Energy in the Far-InfraRed Experiment) mission. The PREFIRE mission, expected to last at least 10 months, consists of sending two CubeSats to synchronous, near-polar orbits, to help close a gap in our understanding of how much of Earth’s heat is lost to space from the Arctic and Antarctica.","keywords":["NASA","PREFIRE","Polar Radiant Energy in the Far InfraRed Experiment","LSP","Launch Services Program","JPL","Jet Propulsion Laboratory","Earth","climate","CubeSat","small satellite","sea ice","melting","global warming","arctic","tropics","poles","Rocket Lab","Electron","New Zealand","Ready Aim PREFIRE","PREFIRE and Ice"],"location":"Rocket Lab, Launch Complex 1, New Zealand","media_type":"video","nasa_id":"KSC-20240525-MH-RKL01-0001-Rocket_Lab_PREFIRE_1_Launch_1080p-M6988","photographer":"Rocket Lab","title":"Rocket Lab PREFIRE-1 Launch"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/video/KSC-20240525-MH-RKL01-0001-Rocket_Lab_PREFIRE_1_Launch_1080p-M6988/KSC-20240525-MH-RKL01-0001-Rocket_Lab_PREFIRE_1_Launch_1080p-M6988~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":800,"size":15000,"height":450},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/video/KSC-20240525-MH-RKL01-0001-Rocket_Lab_PREFIRE_1_Launch_1080p-M6988/KSC-20240525-MH-RKL01-0001-Rocket_Lab_PREFIRE_1_Launch_1080p-M6988~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":400,"size":7000,"height":225},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/video/KSC-20240525-MH-RKL01-0001-Rocket_Lab_PREFIRE_1_Launch_1080p-M6988/KSC-20240525-MH-RKL01-0001-Rocket_Lab_PREFIRE_1_Launch_1080p-M6988~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":200,"size":2900,"height":112},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/video/KSC-20240525-MH-RKL01-0001-Rocket_Lab_PREFIRE_1_Launch_1080p-M6988/KSC-20240525-MH-RKL01-0001-Rocket_Lab_PREFIRE_1_Launch_1080p-M6988~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":300,"size":4800,"height":168},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/video/KSC-20240525-MH-RKL01-0001-Rocket_Lab_PREFIRE_1_Launch_1080p-M6988/KSC-20240525-MH-RKL01-0001-Rocket_Lab_PREFIRE_1_Launch_1080p-M6988.vtt","rel":"captions"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/video/KSC-20240605-MH-RKL01-0001-Rocket_Lab_PREFIRE_and_Ice_Launch_1080p-M6988/collection.json","data":[{"center":"KSC","date_created":"2024-06-05T00:00:00Z","description":"Rocket Lab’s Electron rocket called “PREFIRE and Ice,” lifts off from Launch Complex 1 in Māhia, New Zealand at 3:15 p.m. NZST Wednesday, June 5, 2024 (11:15 p.m. EDT, Tuesday, June 4), on the second of two launches for NASA’s PREFIRE (Polar Radiant Energy in the Far-InfraRed Experiment). The PREFIRE mission, expected to last at least 10 months, consists of sending two CubeSats to asynchronous, near-polar orbits, to help close a gap in our understanding of how much of Earth’s heat is lost to space from the Arctic and Antarctica.","keywords":["NASA","PREFIRE","Polar Radiant Energy in the Far InfraRed Experiment","LSP","Launch Services Program","JPL","Jet Propulsion Laboratory","Earth","climate","CubeSat","small satellite","sea ice","melting","global warming","arctic","tropics","poles","Rocket Lab","Electron","New Zealand","Ready Aim PREFIRE","PREFIRE and Ice"],"location":"Rocket Lab, Launch Complex 1, New Zealand","media_type":"video","nasa_id":"KSC-20240605-MH-RKL01-0001-Rocket_Lab_PREFIRE_and_Ice_Launch_1080p-M6988","photographer":"Rocket Lab","title":"Rocket Lab PREFIRE and Ice Launch"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/video/KSC-20240605-MH-RKL01-0001-Rocket_Lab_PREFIRE_and_Ice_Launch_1080p-M6988/KSC